## What the instructions assume {#what-those-three-instructions-assume .smaller}

::: {.small}
- **'A single, main result'** assumes that one test statistic can stand for the claim, and leaves its degrees of freedom to the software of each analyst
- **'The positive non-materialist form'** is the cosmopolitan scale of the paper. It assumes that the five items form one scale, and that the summary used in the paper, each respondent's share of mentions, is the right one; a mean, a sum or a factor score would all be defensible
- **'The unemployment rate'** assumes that the claim is about unemployment. The abstract of the paper says "poor economic performances" – which also names GDP growth
- **'Disregard contextual variables'** of EU policy and party positions removes the variables of Model 2. Read literally, it leaves the rest of Model 1 to the analyst, yet four of the five fitted unemployment alone
:::

::: {.fragment .small}
None of these is wrong. Each one is a **decision**, made for you, that a different study could reasonably have made differently.
:::

::: notes
Now take the instructions apart, because each rests on an assumption. Asking for a single main result assumes that one test statistic can stand for the claim, and it leaves the degrees of freedom to whatever the software of each analyst reports, which is where the conversion went wrong for one of us. The positive non-materialist form is the cosmopolitan scale, and it takes for granted that the five items – peace, democracy, freedom of movement, cultural diversity, a stronger voice in the world – form one scale, summarised as each respondent's share of mentions. A mean would be defensible, and so would a sum or a factor score. 'The unemployment rate' assumes that the claim is about unemployment, but the abstract says "poor economic performances", which just as clearly names GDP growth – and in the free task three of the five of us used a GDP measure. The last instruction removes the EU-policy and party variables of Model 2. Read literally, it leaves individual controls, growth and the education interactions to us, and four of the five dropped them all. None of these is wrong. Each is a decision, made for you, that another study could reasonably have made differently.
